The key vulnerability I see is in the compressed data path. When reading compressed data, the variable info (dimensions, etc.) is read from the compressed stream. Then when Mat_VarRead5 is called, it allocates memory based on `nelems * data_size` and reads data from the compressed stream.

But wait - for compressed data, the dimensions and data are all in the same compressed stream. The InflateRankDims function reads the rank and dimensions from the compressed stream. Then Mat_VarRead5 allocates based on those dimensions and reads the data from the same compressed stream.

The issue is that the compressed stream is shared - the z_stream state is maintained in matvar->internal->z. So when Mat_VarRead5 is called, it continues reading from where InflateRankDims left off.

